export const meta = {
  name: 'rite-cadence',
  description:
    'Run a HUMAN-AUTHORED, pre-validated wave plan through the plan-first/validate/execute rite cadence: per wave → parallel implementers (disjoint owned files) → ownership check → integration gate → per-ghost commit → reconcile-to-clean → migration reversibility → harden (adversarial review→fix, the child workflow) → commit fixes → exorcise. Whole-rite, GATE-STOPS: runs waves back-to-back, halts before a declared gate (stop_before), returns a resume payload, re-invocable (resume_from). Calls workflow("harden") as its one child (legal one-level nesting). SCOPE: frontend/visual waves AND backend/migration waves. BASELINE: before any wave lands the engine probes EVERY plan gate_cmd on the untouched tree (any plan declaring gate_cmds, frontend-only rites included) and records baseline_red_gates = the commands that exited nonzero WITHOUT naming a test id; at the wave gate such a command is EXCUSED with a warning (completed[].warnings, the run warnings[], the ledger and the completion EVP) instead of escalating a fully-built wave, while a gate green at base, a gate naming test ids, and the engine-appended gates all keep their existing behaviour. baseline_red_gates is its own arg with its own measured flag (baseline_red: [] must not silently assert a probe that never ran) and is passed to harden so the same excusal applies there. Backend waves (wave.backend) get a runner-owned scratch Postgres ({{db_url}} injected into gate_cmds; NOTE the backend test suite may be hermetic (e.g. sqlite) — real Postgres coverage is the engine-owned migrate + pg-smoke + migration-gate + reversibility), a hard ownership check (realized files ⊆ declared), and the drift gate on every wave. Migration waves (wave.migration) additionally require EXACTLY ONE implementer; migration files are RUNTIME-detected (never declared — revision numbers depend on the live head) and reversibility (downgrade to pre-wave head → upgrade → drift gate) runs POST-COMMIT. Every stage is model-pinned (mechanical→sonne